Wealth inequality in the US over the last 40 years is primarily driven by shifts in economic power and policy. A major factor is the decline of labor unions and wage stagnation for the majority of workers, while productivity and capital returns have continued to rise. Furthermore, tax policies have often favored the wealthy, and globalization has allowed for offshoring, which has suppressed wages for lower-skilled domestic labor.<turn|>}
